{
  "_readme": [
    "Domain-EXCLUSIVE vocabulary: words that can only plausibly mean one subject",
    "in a library context. Used ONLY to volunteer a subject librarian for a",
    "question that never names a subject -- 'Mozart Piano Sonata K331 sheet",
    "music' -> Music. The subject string must match the Libraries' own liaisons",
    "page exactly; the PERSON is then looked up live, never hardcoded, so this",
    "file cannot go stale when staff change.",
    "",
    "THE HARD LINE, and the whole reason this file is reviewable data and not",
    "code: never add a word that doubles as ordinary English. 'business',",
    "'art', 'design', 'health', 'management' are banned by construction --",
    "that is the unsolved everyday-word problem, and this list exists to walk",
    "around it rather than into it.",
    "",
    "status: 'active' | 'rejected'. Rejected terms are kept with a reason",
    "rather than deleted, so the record of what a librarian turned down",
    "survives the next person who wants to add it back.",
    "Reviewer: Kevin Messner, sent 2026-08-20.",
    "2026-08-20 additions after testing against the REAL question text, not a paraphrase: 'family history' (the alum's question says that, not 'genealogy') and 'piece of music' (the digitisation question). Both found by re-running the actual traffic; both go to Kevin with the rest."
  ],
